	<p>
		I&rsquo;m Oliver Hitchings &mdash; an IT engineer based in the UK. Online I go by
		<strong>CanYouLikeNot</strong>. I spend most of my free time building with AI: writing autonomous
		agents, wiring up local models, and figuring out where the limits actually are.
	</p>

	<p>
		The main project is <strong>OpenClaw</strong>: a local-first autonomous AI platform that runs
		natively on a Mac Mini (M-series, 64GB RAM) in my flat. It has its own gateway, agents, cron
		jobs, memory store, and channels into Telegram and Discord. It runs Qwen3.6 locally for the
		background work and routes to Codex (via free ChatGPT OAuth) and Claude Opus when it needs the
		big guns. Total cloud cost: $0.
	</p>

	<p>
		Day to day I drive <strong>Claude Code</strong> and the <strong>Codex CLI</strong> for almost
		every coding task. This site is where I write about what works, what doesn&rsquo;t, and what
		feels like it&rsquo;s about to change everything about how engineers actually work.
	</p>

